KZ3 patch 2156: present actual resource geometry and retain scheduled UI-transform ownership.

Copy only compatible resources; scale only supported single-sample float textures.
A failed incompatible scale clears the back buffer instead of recording an invalid copy.
Publish target/image geometry only after a successful non-occluded Present.
Track applied direct-UI factors with always-on surface versions through guarded writes,
whole normalized transfers and accepted movie-overlay captures. Unknown blur/composite
lineage retains explicit legacy mapping; this is not complete cached-UI provenance.

Host controls exercise extracted routing/ownership with resource/window mocks.
Native compile, GPU output, DPI and actual pointer behavior require separate validation.
No internal render-resolution change is introduced by this presentation correction.

